    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d202">

                <pb facs="0480" n="384" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg384"/>

                <head>No. 200.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wing to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Quito,
                                Ecuador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-08-11"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 11, 1873</date>.
                        (Received September 17.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 321.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that the
                    Ecuadorian Congress was convened yesterday, after certain very imposing
                    religious and military displays.</p>
                <p>Per this mail, I shall have the honor to forward a copy of the Presidents message
                    to the Congress. According thereto, the financial outlook of Ecuador is on the
                    ascending scale; and the material development of the country quite
                    promising.</p>
                <p>It will be observed that in the course of the message the President recommends
                    the remission of all duties on machinery imported from the United States.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>RUMSEY WING.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
